<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Which of 100 apps are ready for Composio toolkits?</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Research report on auth, API access, MCP coverage, and build readiness across 100 apps — with evidence, accuracy checks, and honest misses.">
  <style>
    /* Scandinavian Design System: strictly neutral alpha-black on #FFFFFF / alpha-white on #0A0A0A.
       Zero warm/cool gray casts, zero gradients, zero heavy shadows, zero all-caps chrome. */
    :root {
      --canvas: #ffffff;
      --surface: #ffffff;
      --surface-alt: rgb(0 0 0 / 3.5%);
      --surface-row: rgb(0 0 0 / 2.5%);
      --ink-1: #000000;
      --ink-2: rgb(0 0 0 / 64%);
      --ink-3: rgb(0 0 0 / 56%);
      --border: rgb(0 0 0 / 10%);
      --border-strong: rgb(0 0 0 / 18%);
      --hover: rgb(0 0 0 / 5%);
      --pressed: rgb(0 0 0 / 9%);
      --solid-bg: #000000;
      --solid-ink: #ffffff;

      --ok-ink: #15803d;
      --ok-bg: rgb(21 128 61 / 8%);
      --warn-ink: #a16207;
      --warn-bg: rgb(161 98 7 / 9%);
      --err-ink: #b91c1c;
      --err-bg: rgb(185 28 28 / 8%);
      --unk-ink: rgb(0 0 0 / 56%);
      --unk-bg: rgb(0 0 0 / 4%);

      --font-sans: "Inter Variable", "Inter", -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      --font-mono: "JetBrains Mono", ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
      --radius: 8px;
      --radius-pill: 999px;
      --max-w: 1180px;
      --gutter: 48px;
      --toc-w: 220px;
    }

    @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
      :root:not([data-theme="light"]) {
        --canvas: #0a0a0a;
        --surface: #121212;
        --surface-alt: rgb(255 255 255 / 4.5%);
        --surface-row: rgb(255 255 255 / 3%);
        --ink-1: #ffffff;
        --ink-2: rgb(255 255 255 / 56%);
        --ink-3: rgb(255 255 255 / 46%);
        --border: rgb(255 255 255 / 11%);
        --border-strong: rgb(255 255 255 / 20%);
        --hover: rgb(255 255 255 / 9%);
        --pressed: rgb(255 255 255 / 14%);
        --solid-bg: #ffffff;
        --solid-ink: #0a0a0a;
        --ok-ink: #4ade80;
        --ok-bg: rgb(74 222 128 / 12%);
        --warn-ink: #fbbf24;
        --warn-bg: rgb(251 191 36 / 12%);
        --err-ink: #f87171;
        --err-bg: rgb(248 113 113 / 12%);
        --unk-ink: rgb(255 255 255 / 50%);
        --unk-bg: rgb(255 255 255 / 6%);
      }
    }

    :root[data-theme="dark"] {
      --canvas: #0a0a0a;
      --surface: #121212;
      --surface-alt: rgb(255 255 255 / 4.5%);
      --surface-row: rgb(255 255 255 / 3%);
      --ink-1: #ffffff;
      --ink-2: rgb(255 255 255 / 56%);
      --ink-3: rgb(255 255 255 / 46%);
      --border: rgb(255 255 255 / 11%);
      --border-strong: rgb(255 255 255 / 20%);
      --hover: rgb(255 255 255 / 9%);
      --pressed: rgb(255 255 255 / 14%);
      --solid-bg: #ffffff;
      --solid-ink: #0a0a0a;
      --ok-ink: #4ade80;
      --ok-bg: rgb(74 222 128 / 12%);
      --warn-ink: #fbbf24;
      --warn-bg: rgb(251 191 36 / 12%);
      --err-ink: #f87171;
      --err-bg: rgb(248 113 113 / 12%);
      --unk-ink: rgb(255 255 255 / 50%);
      --unk-bg: rgb(255 255 255 / 6%);
    }

    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      html { scroll-behavior: auto; }
      *, *::before, *::after { transition-duration: 0.01ms !important; animation-duration: 0.01ms !important; }
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      background: var(--canvas);
      color: var(--ink-1);
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-size: 16px;
      line-height: 1.55;
      -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      overflow-x: hidden;
    }

    a { color: var(--ink-1); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: var(--border-strong); text-underline-offset: 3px; }
    a:hover { text-decoration-color: var(--ink-1); }
    :focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--ink-1); outline-offset: 2px; border-radius: 4px; }

    .wrap { max-width: var(--max-w); margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 var(--gutter); }

    .topbar {
      position: sticky;
      top: 0;
      z-index: 40;
      background: var(--canvas);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .topbar-inner {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 16px;
      min-height: 52px;
      padding: 8px 0;
    }
    .brand {
      font-size: 14px;
      font-weight: 500;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      text-decoration: none;
      color: var(--ink-1);
    }
    .brand-meta {
      font-size: 13px;
      color: var(--ink-3);
      font-weight: 400;
      margin-left: 10px;
    }
    .topbar-actions {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
    .export-links {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 6px;
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 12px;
    }
    .export-links a {
      text-decoration: none;
      color: var(--ink-2);
      padding: 4px 8px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
    }
    .export-links a:hover { color: var(--ink-1); border-color: var(--border-strong); background: var(--hover); }

    button, select, input {
      font-family: inherit;
      font-size: 14px;
      color: var(--ink-1);
    }
    .btn {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      height: 34px;
      padding: 0 12px;
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 500;
      background: transparent;
      border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      cursor: pointer;
    }
    .btn:hover { background: var(--hover); }
    .btn:active { background: var(--pressed); }
    .btn--solid {
      background: var(--solid-bg);
      color: var(--solid-ink);
      border-color: var(--solid-bg);
    }
    .btn--solid:hover { opacity: 0.9; background: var(--solid-bg); }

    /* Report cover */
    .cover {
      padding: 72px 0 48px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .cover-kicker {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 500;
      color: var(--ink-3);
      margin: 0 0 16px;
    }
    .cover h1 {
      margin: 0 0 16px;
      font-size: clamp(28px, 3.6vw, 40px);
      font-weight: 500;
      line-height: 1.12;
      letter-spacing: -0.025em;
      max-width: 22ch;
    }
    .cover-lead {
      margin: 0 0 28px;
      font-size: 17px;
      color: var(--ink-2);
      max-width: 62ch;
    }
    .cover-meta {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 20px 28px;
      padding-top: 24px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      max-width: 820px;
    }
    .meta-label {
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 500;
      color: var(--ink-3);
      margin-bottom: 4px;
    }
    .meta-value {
      font-size: 14px;
      font-weight: 500;
      color: var(--ink-1);
    }

    /* Report shell: sticky ToC + body */
    .report-shell {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: var(--toc-w) minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 48px;
      align-items: start;
      padding: 40px 0 0;
    }
    .toc {
      position: sticky;
      top: 68px;
      padding-bottom: 40px;
      max-height: 720px;
      overflow-y: auto;
    }
    .toc-label {
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 500;
      color: var(--ink-3);
      margin: 0 0 12px;
    }
    .toc ol {
      list-style: none;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
    }
    .toc li { margin: 0; }
    .toc a {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 28px minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 8px;
      padding: 8px 0;
      text-decoration: none;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
      color: var(--ink-2);
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 500;
      line-height: 1.35;
    }
    .toc a:hover { color: var(--ink-1); background: var(--hover); }
    .toc-num {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 12px;
      color: var(--ink-3);
    }
    .toc-desc {
      display: block;
      margin-top: 2px;
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 400;
      color: var(--ink-3);
    }
    .report-body { min-width: 0; padding-bottom: 48px; }

    .chapter {
      padding: 56px 0;
      scroll-margin-top: 72px;
    }
    .chapter + .chapter { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
    .chapter-head { max-width: 68ch; margin-bottom: 28px; }
    .chapter-num {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 500;
      color: var(--ink-3);
      margin-bottom: 8px;
    }
    h2 {
      margin: 0 0 10px;
      font-size: clamp(22px, 2.4vw, 28px);
      font-weight: 500;
      line-height: 1.15;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    }
    h3 {
      margin: 0 0 8px;
      font-size: 16px;
      font-weight: 500;
      line-height: 1.3;
    }
    .lead { margin: 0; font-size: 15px; color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 64ch; }

    .kpi-strip {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 24px;
      padding: 24px 0;
      margin: 0 0 36px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .kpi-val {
      font-size: clamp(22px, 2.4vw, 30px);
      font-weight: 500;
      line-height: 1.1;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    }
    .kpi-label {
      margin-top: 6px;
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 500;
      color: var(--ink-2);
    }
    .kpi-note {
      margin-top: 2px;
      font-size: 12px;
      color: var(--ink-3);
    }

    .headline-list {
      list-style: none;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 28px 40px;
    }
    .headline-item {
      display: flex;
      gap: 14px;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }
    .headline-idx {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 500;
      color: var(--ink-3);
      min-width: 24px;
      padding-top: 2px;
    }
    .headline-title {
      font-size: 15px;
      font-weight: 500;
      margin: 0 0 4px;
    }
    .headline-text {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 14px;
      color: var(--ink-2);
    }

    .bucket-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 32px;
    }
    .bucket-col {
      padding-top: 16px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    }
    .bucket-head {
      display: flex;
      align-items: baseline;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 12px;
      margin-bottom: 6px;
    }
    .bucket-count {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 20px;
      font-weight: 500;
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    }
    .bucket-desc {
      margin: 0 0 16px;
      font-size: 13px;
      color: var(--ink-2);
    }
    .chip-wrap {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 6px;
    }
    .chip {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 6px;
      padding: 4px 10px;
      font-size: 12.5px;
      font-weight: 500;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
      background: var(--surface);
      color: var(--ink-1);
      cursor: pointer;
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    .chip:hover { border-color: var(--border-strong); background: var(--hover); }
    .chip--gap {
      background: var(--solid-bg);
      color: var(--solid-ink);
      border-color: var(--solid-bg);
    }
    .chip--gap:hover { opacity: 0.88; background: var(--solid-bg); }
    .chip--hidden { display: none; }
    .chip-score {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 11px;
      opacity: 0.72;
    }
    .legend-row {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 20px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
      font-size: 13px;
      color: var(--ink-2);
    }
    .legend-swatch {
      display: inline-block;
      width: 10px;
      height: 10px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      margin-right: 6px;
      vertical-align: middle;
    }

    .view-tools {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 10px 16px;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
      padding: 12px 14px;
      background: var(--surface-alt);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
    }
    .view-tools label {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 500;
      color: var(--ink-2);
      cursor: pointer;
    }
    .view-tools input[type="checkbox"] {
      width: 14px;
      height: 14px;
      accent-color: var(--ink-1);
    }
    .view-tools select {
      height: 32px;
      padding: 0 8px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      background: var(--surface);
    }
    .view-tools .tool-group {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px 14px;
    }
    .view-tools .tool-sep {
      width: 1px;
      height: 20px;
      background: var(--border-strong);
    }

    .chart-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 36px 40px;
      margin-bottom: 40px;
    }
    .chart-block[hidden] { display: none; }
    .chart-block h3 { margin-bottom: 4px; }
    .chart-sub { margin: 0 0 16px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-2); }
    .bar-row {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 150px minmax(0, 1fr) 44px;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 12px;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
      font-size: 13px;
    }
    .bar-label { color: var(--ink-2); overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
    .bar-track {
      height: 10px;
      background: var(--hover);
      border-radius: 3px;
      overflow: hidden;
    }
    .bar-fill {
      height: 100%;
      background: var(--ink-1);
      border-radius: 3px;
    }
    .bar-fill--muted { background: var(--ink-3); }
    .bar-val {
      text-align: right;
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 12.5px;
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
      color: var(--ink-1);
    }

    .split-2 > *, .bucket-grid > *, .chart-grid > *, .detail-grid > *, .kpi-strip > *, .headline-list > *, .cover-meta > * {
      min-width: 0;
    }

    .table-wrap {
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 100%;
      overflow-x: auto;
      -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
    }
    table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      text-align: left;
      font-size: 13.5px;
    }
    th {
      font-size: 12.5px;
      font-weight: 500;
      color: var(--ink-2);
      padding: 10px 12px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
    td {
      padding: 10px 12px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
      vertical-align: top;
    }
    .num {
      text-align: right;
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    }
    .heat-cell {
      text-align: center;
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 12.5px;
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
      border-radius: 4px;
    }
    th.col-hidden, td.col-hidden { display: none; }

    .badge {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 6px;
      padding: 2px 8px;
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 500;
      border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
    .badge::before {
      content: "";
      width: 6px;
      height: 6px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: currentColor;
      flex-shrink: 0;
    }
    .badge--ok { color: var(--ok-ink); background: var(--ok-bg); }
    .badge--warn { color: var(--warn-ink); background: var(--warn-bg); }
    .badge--err { color: var(--err-ink); background: var(--err-bg); }
    .badge--unk { color: var(--unk-ink); background: var(--unk-bg); border: 1px dashed var(--border-strong); }
    .badge--solid { color: var(--solid-ink); background: var(--solid-bg); }
    .badge--solid::before { display: none; }

    .filter-bar {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(160px, 1fr));
      gap: 10px;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
    }
    .filter-bar input, .filter-bar select {
      height: 36px;
      padding: 0 10px;
      background: var(--surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      width: 100%;
    }
    .filter-meta {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 12px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
      font-size: 13px;
      color: var(--ink-2);
    }
    .filter-meta .actions {
      display: flex;
      gap: 8px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }

    .exp-row { cursor: pointer; }
    .exp-row:nth-child(4n+1) { background: var(--surface-row); }
    .exp-row:hover { background: var(--hover); }
    .exp-detail { display: none; background: var(--surface-alt); }
    .exp-detail.is-open { display: table-row; }
    .detail-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.5fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 28px;
      padding: 16px 8px;
    }
    .claim-item {
      padding: 10px 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .claim-item:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
    .claim-top {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 8px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      margin-bottom: 4px;
    }
    .claim-name { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 500; }
    .claim-val { font-size: 13.5px; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 4px; }
    .claim-quote {
      margin: 4px 0;
      padding-left: 10px;
      border-left: 2px solid var(--border-strong);
      font-size: 12.5px;
      color: var(--ink-2);
    }
    .claim-meta { font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-3); word-break: break-word; }

    .split-2 {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 36px 40px;
      margin-top: 28px;
    }

    details {
      margin-top: 20px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      padding-top: 12px;
    }
    summary {
      cursor: pointer;
      font-size: 14px;
      font-weight: 500;
      color: var(--ink-1);
      padding: 4px 0;
    }

    pre {
      margin: 12px 0 0;
      padding: 16px;
      background: var(--surface-alt);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 12.5px;
      line-height: 1.5;
      overflow-x: auto;
    }
    code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.9em; }

    .pipeline-wrap {
      width: 100%;
      overflow-x: auto;
      margin: 8px 0 32px;
      padding: 20px 16px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      background: var(--surface-alt);
    }
    .pipeline-svg {
      display: block;
      width: 100%;
      min-width: 760px;
      height: auto;
      color: var(--ink-1);
    }
    .arch-legend {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 16px 24px;
      margin: -16px 0 28px;
      font-size: 13px;
      color: var(--ink-2);
    }

    footer {
      padding: 32px 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      font-size: 13px;
      color: var(--ink-2);
    }
    .footer-inner {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 16px;
    }

    @media (max-width: 980px) {
      :root { --gutter: 24px; }
      .report-shell { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0; padding-top: 16px; }
      .toc {
        position: static;
        max-height: none;
        margin-bottom: 8px;
        padding: 16px;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        background: var(--surface-alt);
      }
      .toc ol {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
        gap: 0 16px;
      }
      .toc a { border-bottom: none; padding: 6px 0; }
      .toc-desc { display: none; }
      .cover { padding: 48px 0 32px; }
      .cover-meta { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
      .chapter { padding: 40px 0; }
      .kpi-strip { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
      .headline-list, .bucket-grid, .chart-grid, .split-2, .detail-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .brand-meta { display: none; }
    }
    @media (max-width: 560px) {
      .cover-meta, .kpi-strip { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .toc ol { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .bar-row { grid-template-columns: 112px minmax(0, 1fr) 36px; }
      .view-tools .tool-sep { display: none; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="topbar">
    <div class="wrap topbar-inner">
      <a class="brand" href="#cover">App Intelligence Audit <span class="brand-meta">Report</span></a>
      <div class="topbar-actions">
        <div class="export-links" aria-label="Download the dataset">
          <a href="apps.json" title="Full dataset as JSON">JSON</a>
          <a href="apps.csv" title="Full dataset as CSV">CSV</a>
          <a href="llms.txt" title="Machine-readable summary">Guide</a>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="btn" id="theme-toggle" aria-label="Toggle light and dark theme">Theme</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section id="cover" class="cover">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="cover-kicker">Composio · App research report</p>
        <h1>Which of {{ analytics.summary.total_apps }} apps are ready to turn into agent tools?</h1>
        <p class="cover-lead">
          Composio turns apps into tools AI agents can call. Before building a toolkit, you need to know how each app authenticates, whether a developer can sign up alone, what the API looks like, and what blocks shipping.
          I researched all {{ analytics.summary.total_apps }} apps with an agent, checked every answer against the docs, and ranked what is ready to build versus what needs outreach.
        </p>
        <div class="cover-meta">
          <div>
            <div class="meta-label">What I studied</div>
            <div class="meta-value">{{ analytics.summary.total_apps }} apps across 10 categories</div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="meta-label">How I worked</div>
            <div class="meta-value">Agent research, then six automated checks</div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="meta-label">Hand-checked accuracy</div>
            <div class="meta-value">{{ "%.0f"|format(acc1.overall.accuracy) }}% draft → {{ "%.0f"|format(acc2.overall.accuracy) }}% after checks → {{ "%.0f"|format(accf.overall.accuracy) }}% final</div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="meta-label">Already in Composio</div>
            <div class="meta-value">{{ analytics.summary.composio_available }} of {{ analytics.summary.total_apps }} apps</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="wrap report-shell">
      <nav class="toc" id="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
        <p class="toc-label">Contents</p>
        <ol>
          <li><a href="#headlines"><span class="toc-num">01</span><span>Key findings<span class="toc-desc">Patterns across all 100 apps</span></span></a></li>
          <li><a href="#opportunities"><span class="toc-num">02</span><span>What to build next<span class="toc-desc">Easy wins vs outreach</span></span></a></li>
          <li><a href="#patterns"><span class="toc-num">03</span><span>Charts<span class="toc-desc">Auth, access, and MCP</span></span></a></li>
          <li><a href="#explorer"><span class="toc-num">04</span><span>All {{ analytics.summary.total_apps }} apps<span class="toc-desc">Filter and open the evidence</span></span></a></li>
          <li><a href="#verification"><span class="toc-num">05</span><span>How I checked accuracy<span class="toc-desc">Hand sample and automated checks</span></span></a></li>
          <li><a href="#wrong"><span class="toc-num">06</span><span>Where I was wrong<span class="toc-desc">Honest misses and hard apps</span></span></a></li>
          <li><a href="#architecture"><span class="toc-num">07</span><span>How the agent works<span class="toc-desc">Pipeline and human steps</span></span></a></li>
          <li><a href="#reproduce"><span class="toc-num">08</span><span>Try it yourself<span class="toc-desc">Live run link and source</span></span></a></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <div class="report-body">
        <!-- 1. Headline patterns -->
        <section id="headlines" class="chapter">
          <div class="chapter-head">
            <div class="chapter-num">01 / Key findings</div>
            <h2>What stands out across all {{ analytics.summary.total_apps }} apps</h2>
            <p class="lead">
              Six patterns computed from the full dataset. Every number on this page comes from the research results — nothing was typed in by hand.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="kpi-strip">
            <div>
              <div class="kpi-val">{{ analytics.summary.total_apps }}</div>
              <div class="kpi-label">Apps researched</div>
              <div class="kpi-note">10 categories · {{ analytics.summary.composio_available }} already in Composio</div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="kpi-val">{{ analytics.summary.self_serve_free }}%</div>
              <div class="kpi-label">Free developer signup</div>
              <div class="kpi-note">{{ analytics.distributions.production_gate.gated_despite_free_dev }} of those still need approval to ship</div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="kpi-val">{{ analytics.summary.oauth2_supported }}%</div>
              <div class="kpi-label">Support OAuth 2.0</div>
              <div class="kpi-note">{{ analytics.distributions.auth_methods.multi_method_apps }} offer more than one auth method</div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="kpi-val">
                {{ "%.0f"|format(acc1.overall.accuracy) }}% → {{ "%.0f"|format(acc2.overall.accuracy) }}% → {{ "%.0f"|format(accf.overall.accuracy) }}%
              </div>
              <div class="kpi-label">Accuracy on a hand-checked sample</div>
              <div class="kpi-note">20 apps · draft → after checks → final after my edits</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <ol class="headline-list">
            {% for h in analytics.headlines %}
            <li class="headline-item">
              <span class="headline-idx">0{{ loop.index }}</span>
              <div>
                <div class="headline-title">{{ h.title }}</div>
                <p class="headline-text">{{ h.text }}</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ol>
        </section>

        <!-- 2. Opportunity matrix -->
        <section id="opportunities" class="chapter">
          <div class="chapter-head">
            <div class="chapter-num">02 / What to build next</div>
            <h2>Ready to build, needs outreach, or blocked</h2>
            <p class="lead">
              Each app gets a readiness score from 0–10 based on docs quality, auth, how you get credentials, API surface, and MCP. If the vendor requires a partnership or sales contact, the app lands in “Needs outreach” even when the API is strong. Click any app to see the evidence.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="view-tools" role="group" aria-label="Opportunity view controls">
            <label><input type="checkbox" id="opp-gaps-only"> Show only apps not yet in Composio</label>
            <span class="tool-sep" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <div class="tool-group">
              <label for="opp-bucket-filter">Show</label>
              <select id="opp-bucket-filter" aria-label="Filter opportunity buckets">
                <option value="">All groups</option>
                <option value="easy">Easy wins</option>
                <option value="outreach">Needs outreach</option>
                <option value="moderate">Moderate effort</option>
                <option value="blocked">Technically blocked</option>
              </select>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="legend-row">
            <span><span class="legend-swatch" style="background: var(--solid-bg);"></span>Not in Composio yet</span>
            <span><span class="legend-swatch" style="border: 1px solid var(--border-strong); background: var(--surface);"></span>Already in Composio</span>
          </div>

          <div class="bucket-grid">
            <div class="bucket-col" data-opp-bucket="easy">
              <div class="bucket-head">
                <h3>Easy wins</h3>
                <span class="bucket-count" data-opp-count>{{ analytics.opportunities.easy_wins_all|length }}</span>
              </div>
              <p class="bucket-desc">
                Score 8–10 and no partnership wall. <strong>{{ analytics.opportunities.easy_wins_without_composio|length }} are not in Composio yet</strong> — the clearest places to build next.
              </p>
              <div class="chip-wrap">
                {% for a in analytics.opportunities.easy_wins_all %}
                <button type="button" class="chip {% if a.composio_toolkit != 'available' %}chip--gap{% endif %}" data-jump-app="{{ a.app_id }}" data-composio="{{ a.composio_toolkit }}" title="Score {{ a.score }}/10 · {{ a.category }} · Composio: {{ a.composio_toolkit }}">
                  {{ a.app }} <span class="chip-score">{{ a.score }}</span>
                </button>
                {% endfor %}
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="bucket-col" data-opp-bucket="outreach">
              <div class="bucket-head">
                <h3>Needs outreach</h3>
                <span class="bucket-count" data-opp-count>{{ analytics.opportunities.outreach_targets|length }}</span>
              </div>
              <p class="bucket-desc">
                Vendor requires a partnership, sales contact, or partner program. <strong>{{ analytics.opportunities.outreach_without_composio|length }} are not in Composio yet</strong>.
              </p>
              <div class="chip-wrap">
                {% for a in analytics.opportunities.outreach_targets %}
                <button type="button" class="chip {% if a.composio_toolkit != 'available' %}chip--gap{% endif %}" data-jump-app="{{ a.app_id }}" data-composio="{{ a.composio_toolkit }}" title="Score {{ a.score }}/10 · {{ a.credential_access }} / {{ a.production_gate }}">
                  {{ a.app }} <span class="chip-score">{{ a.score }}</span>
                </button>
                {% endfor %}
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="bucket-col" data-opp-bucket="moderate">
              <div class="bucket-head">
                <h3>Moderate effort</h3>
                <span class="bucket-count" data-opp-count>{{ analytics.opportunities.moderate|length }}</span>
              </div>
              <p class="bucket-desc">
                Score 5–7: doable, but expect paid plans, a narrower API, a CLI wrapper, or no official MCP server.
              </p>
              <div class="chip-wrap">
                {% for a in analytics.opportunities.moderate %}
                <button type="button" class="chip {% if a.composio_toolkit != 'available' %}chip--gap{% endif %}" data-jump-app="{{ a.app_id }}" data-composio="{{ a.composio_toolkit }}" title="Score {{ a.score }}/10 · {{ a.category }}">
                  {{ a.app }} <span class="chip-score">{{ a.score }}</span>
                </button>
                {% endfor %}
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="bucket-col" data-opp-bucket="blocked">
              <div class="bucket-head">
                <h3>Technically blocked</h3>
                <span class="bucket-count" data-opp-count>{{ analytics.opportunities.technically_blocked|length }}</span>
              </div>
              <p class="bucket-desc">
                Score 0–4: little or no public API documentation, or specs locked behind an NDA.
              </p>
              <div class="chip-wrap">
                {% for a in analytics.opportunities.technically_blocked %}
                <button type="button" class="chip {% if a.composio_toolkit != 'available' %}chip--gap{% endif %}" data-jump-app="{{ a.app_id }}" data-composio="{{ a.composio_toolkit }}" title="Score {{ a.score }}/10 · {{ a.main_blocker_text }}">
                  {{ a.app }} <span class="chip-score">{{ a.score }}</span>
                </button>
                {% endfor %}
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 3. Pattern charts -->
        <section id="patterns" class="chapter">
          <div class="chapter-head">
            <div class="chapter-num">03 / Charts</div>
            <h2>How auth and access break down</h2>
            <p class="lead">
              Toggle charts on or off to focus on what you care about. Every chart is built from the same {{ analytics.summary.total_apps }}-app dataset on this page.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="view-tools" role="group" aria-label="Chart visibility">
            <span class="tool-group">
              <label><input type="checkbox" class="chart-toggle" data-chart="auth" checked> How apps authenticate</label>
              <label><input type="checkbox" class="chart-toggle" data-chart="access" checked> How you get credentials</label>
              <label><input type="checkbox" class="chart-toggle" data-chart="gate" checked> Extra gates to ship</label>
              <label><input type="checkbox" class="chart-toggle" data-chart="mcp" checked> MCP &amp; Composio</label>
              <label><input type="checkbox" id="heatmap-toggle" checked> Category heatmap</label>
            </span>
          </div>

          <div class="chart-grid" id="pattern-charts"></div>

          <div id="heatmap-block">
            <h3>By category: how hard is it to get credentials?</h3>
            <p class="chart-sub">Each category has 10 apps. Darker cells mean more apps in that access tier.</p>
            <div class="table-wrap" id="heatmap-wrap"></div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 4. Findings explorer -->
        <section id="explorer" class="chapter">
          <div class="chapter-head">
            <div class="chapter-num">04 / All {{ analytics.summary.total_apps }} apps</div>
            <h2>Browse every app and open the source behind each answer</h2>
            <p class="lead">
              Filter and sort to focus the table. Click a row to see the docs quote and URL for each fact, plus how the readiness score was calculated. Values the agent could not confirm are marked unknown.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="filter-bar">
            <input type="search" id="f-search" placeholder="Search by app, category, or blocker..." aria-label="Search apps">
            <select id="f-category" aria-label="Filter by category"><option value="">All categories</option></select>
            <select id="f-bucket" aria-label="Filter by group">
              <option value="">All groups</option>
              <option value="easy_win">Easy win</option>
              <option value="moderate">Moderate</option>
              <option value="needs_outreach">Needs outreach</option>
              <option value="technically_blocked">Technically blocked</option>
            </select>
            <select id="f-verdict" aria-label="Filter by score band">
              <option value="">All score bands</option>
              <option value="easy">Easy (8–10)</option>
              <option value="moderate">Moderate (5–7)</option>
              <option value="difficult">Difficult (3–4)</option>
              <option value="blocked">Blocked (0–2)</option>
            </select>
            <select id="f-auth" aria-label="Filter by auth method"><option value="">All auth methods</option></select>
            <select id="f-access" aria-label="Filter by how you get credentials"><option value="">Any credential path</option></select>
            <select id="f-gate" aria-label="Filter by ship gate"><option value="">Any ship gate</option></select>
            <select id="f-api" aria-label="Filter by API type"><option value="">All API types</option></select>
            <select id="f-mcp" aria-label="Filter by official MCP">
              <option value="">Any official MCP</option>
              <option value="yes">Has official MCP</option>
              <option value="no_found">No official MCP found</option>
              <option value="unknown">Official MCP unknown</option>
            </select>
            <select id="f-composio" aria-label="Filter by Composio coverage">
              <option value="">Any Composio status</option>
              <option value="available">In Composio</option>
              <option value="unavailable">Not in Composio</option>
            </select>
            <select id="f-vstatus" aria-label="Filter by evidence strength">
              <option value="">Any evidence strength</option>
              <option value="all_supported">All known answers fully supported</option>
              <option value="has_flagged">Has weak or disputed evidence</option>
            </select>
          </div>

          <div class="view-tools" role="group" aria-label="Explorer view controls">
            <div class="tool-group">
              <label for="f-sort">Sort</label>
              <select id="f-sort" aria-label="Sort explorer rows">
                <option value="id-asc">App id ↑</option>
                <option value="id-desc">App id ↓</option>
                <option value="score-desc">Score ↓</option>
                <option value="score-asc">Score ↑</option>
                <option value="name-asc">Name A–Z</option>
                <option value="name-desc">Name Z–A</option>
                <option value="category-asc">Category A–Z</option>
              </select>
            </div>
            <span class="tool-sep" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <div class="tool-group" id="col-toggles" aria-label="Column visibility">
              <label><input type="checkbox" class="col-toggle" data-col="score" checked> Score</label>
              <label><input type="checkbox" class="col-toggle" data-col="bucket" checked> Group</label>
              <label><input type="checkbox" class="col-toggle" data-col="auth" checked> Auth</label>
              <label><input type="checkbox" class="col-toggle" data-col="access" checked> Credentials</label>
              <label><input type="checkbox" class="col-toggle" data-col="gate" checked> Ship gate</label>
              <label><input type="checkbox" class="col-toggle" data-col="mcp" checked> MCP</label>
              <label><input type="checkbox" class="col-toggle" data-col="composio" checked> Composio</label>
              <label><input type="checkbox" class="col-toggle" data-col="confidence" checked> Confidence</label>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="filter-meta">
            <span id="explorer-count">Showing 100 of 100 apps</span>
            <div class="actions">
              <button type="button" class="btn" id="f-export">Download this view as CSV</button>
              <button type="button" class="btn" id="f-reset">Clear filters</button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="table-wrap">
            <table id="explorer-table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th data-col="id">#</th>
                  <th data-col="app">App</th>
                  <th data-col="category">Category</th>
                  <th class="num" data-col="score">Score</th>
                  <th data-col="bucket">Group</th>
                  <th data-col="auth">Auth</th>
                  <th data-col="access">Credentials</th>
                  <th data-col="gate">Ship gate</th>
                  <th data-col="mcp">Official MCP</th>
                  <th data-col="composio">In Composio?</th>
                  <th data-col="confidence">Confidence</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody id="explorer-body"></tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 5. Verification -->
        <section id="verification" class="chapter">
          {% set field_labels = {
            "auth_methods": "Auth methods",
            "credential_access": "How you get credentials",
            "production_gate": "Extra gate to ship",
            "api_type": "API type",
            "mcp_official": "Official MCP",
            "main_blocker_type": "Main blocker"
          } %}
          {% set loop_labels = {
            "L1": "Schema & consistency",
            "L2": "Docs link still works",
            "L3": "Quote matches the page",
            "L4": "Re-read page in a browser",
            "L5": "Second model reviews the claim",
            "L6": "Targeted re-research"
          } %}
          <div class="chapter-head">
            <div class="chapter-num">05 / How I checked accuracy</div>
            <h2>I labelled 20 apps by hand; automation improved the draft</h2>
            <p class="lead">
              I hand-checked 20 apps (120 facts) against the real docs. The agent’s first draft scored {{ "%.0f"|format(acc1.overall.accuracy) }}%. After six automated checks it rose to {{ "%.0f"|format(acc2.overall.accuracy) }}%. The final {{ "%.0f"|format(accf.overall.accuracy) }}% figure includes my corrections and is labelled separately so the automated gain stays honest.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="split-2">
            <div>
              <h3>Accuracy by fact type</h3>
              <p class="chart-sub">20 hand-checked apps × 6 facts each = 120 answers.</p>
              <div class="table-wrap">
                <table>
                  <thead>
                    <tr>
                      <th>Fact</th>
                      <th class="num">First draft</th>
                      <th class="num">After checks</th>
                      <th class="num">Change</th>
                      <th class="num">Final (my edits)</th>
                    </tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody>
                    {% for fname in acc1.per_field.keys() %}
                    {% set p1 = acc1.per_field[fname].accuracy %}
                    {% set p2 = acc2.per_field[fname].accuracy %}
                    {% set pf = accf.per_field[fname].accuracy %}
                    {% set diff = p2 - p1 %}
                    <tr>
                      <td>{{ field_labels.get(fname, fname) }}</td>
                      <td class="num">{{ "%.0f"|format(p1) }}%</td>
                      <td class="num">{{ "%.0f"|format(p2) }}%</td>
                      <td class="num">{% if diff > 0 %}+{% endif %}{{ "%.1f"|format(diff) }} pts</td>
                      <td class="num">{{ "%.0f"|format(pf) }}%</td>
                    </tr>
                    {% endfor %}
                    <tr style="font-weight: 500;">
                      <td>Overall (120 answers)</td>
                      <td class="num">{{ "%.0f"|format(acc1.overall.accuracy) }}%</td>
                      <td class="num">{{ "%.0f"|format(acc2.overall.accuracy) }}%</td>
                      <td class="num">+{{ "%.1f"|format(acc2.overall.accuracy - acc1.overall.accuracy) }} pts</td>
                      <td class="num">{{ "%.0f"|format(accf.overall.accuracy) }}%</td>
                    </tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3>What each automated check did</h3>
              <p class="chart-sub">Ran on every fact across all 100 apps. “Sample fixes” counts how many hand-checked answers that check improved.</p>
              <div class="table-wrap">
                <table>
                  <thead>
                    <tr>
                      <th>Check</th>
                      <th class="num">Reviewed</th>
                      <th class="num">Flagged</th>
                      <th class="num">Changed</th>
                      <th class="num">Sample fixes</th>
                    </tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody>
                    {% for lp in ["L1", "L2", "L3", "L4", "L5", "L6"] %}
                    {% set d = loop_stats.all_claims.loops[lp] %}
                    <tr>
                      <td>{{ loop_labels[lp] }}</td>
                      <td class="num">{{ d.claims_checked }}</td>
                      <td class="num">{{ d.flagged }}</td>
                      <td class="num">{{ d.values_changed }}</td>
                      <td class="num">{{ attribution.errors_caught_per_loop.credited[lp] }}</td>
                    </tr>
                    {% endfor %}
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
              <p class="kpi-note" style="margin-top: 10px;">
                On the hand-checked sample, automated checks fixed {{ attribution.transitions.fixed or 0 }} answers, made {{ attribution.transitions.regressed or 0 }} worse, filled {{ attribution.transitions.abstained_to_wrong or 0 }} previous unknowns incorrectly, and left {{ attribution.transitions.unchanged_correct or 0 }} already-correct answers alone.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="split-2">
            <div>
              <h3>Apps left out of the hand-checked sample</h3>
              <p class="headline-text">{{ analytics.holdout.note }}</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>What changed between draft and checked results</h3>
              <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 18px; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--ink-2);">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 6px;">I corrected FanBasis / Commas domain redirects after confirming the rebrand in public docs.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 6px;">I added six automated checks (schema, live links, quote matching, browser re-read, second-model review, and targeted re-research).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 6px;">I did not retune the first-draft research prompts against the hand-checked answers — verification was added as a separate stage.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 6px;">Overall sample accuracy rose from {{ "%.1f"|format(acc1.overall.accuracy) }}% to {{ "%.1f"|format(acc2.overall.accuracy) }}% before any human edits to the final dataset.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <details>
            <summary>Every hand-checked answer (120 rows) — draft vs checked vs human label</summary>
            <div style="margin: 12px 0;">
              <select id="golden-filter" aria-label="Filter hand-checked answers" style="height: 34px; padding: 0 10px; border: 1px solid var(--border-strong); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--surface);">
                <option value="all">All 120 answers</option>
                <option value="fixed">Fixed by checks ({{ attribution.transitions.fixed or 0 }})</option>
                <option value="regressed">Made worse by checks ({{ attribution.transitions.regressed or 0 }})</option>
                <option value="abstained_to_wrong">Unknown filled incorrectly ({{ attribution.transitions.abstained_to_wrong or 0 }})</option>
                <option value="misses">Still wrong after checks</option>
              </select>
            </div>
            <div class="table-wrap">
              <table>
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>App</th>
                    <th>Fact</th>
                    <th>My label</th>
                    <th>First draft</th>
                    <th>After checks</th>
                    <th>What happened</th>
                    <th>Which checks</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody id="golden-body"></tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>Technical change log (for engineers who want the file-level detail)</summary>
            <ul style="margin: 12px 0 0; padding-left: 18px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-2);">
              {% for ch in changes %}
              <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;">{{ ch.text }}</li>
              {% endfor %}
            </ul>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- 6. Where I was wrong -->
        <section id="wrong" class="chapter">
          <div class="chapter-head">
            <div class="chapter-num">06 / Where I was wrong</div>
            <h2>Mistakes I’m not hiding</h2>
            <p class="lead">
              Automated checks raised sample accuracy by {{ "%.1f"|format(acc2.overall.accuracy - acc1.overall.accuracy) }} points, but also made {{ wrong.regressions|length }} previously correct answers worse and filled {{ wrong.abstained_to_wrong|length }} unknowns with the wrong value. {{ wrong.total_corrections }} hand-checked facts still needed me to edit the final dataset.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="split-2">
            <div>
              <h3>Made worse by automated checks ({{ wrong.regressions|length }})</h3>
              <p class="chart-sub">These were correct in the first draft. Re-research replaced a full auth list with a narrower answer from a different docs page.</p>
              <div class="table-wrap">
                <table>
                  <thead>
                    <tr><th>App</th><th>Fact</th><th>Draft → after checks</th><th>My label</th></tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody>
                    {% for r in wrong.regressions %}
                    <tr>
                      <td>{{ r.app }}</td>
                      <td>{{ r.field.replace('_', ' ') }}</td>
                      <td>{{ r.before_value }} → {{ r.after_value }}</td>
                      <td>{{ r.golden }}</td>
                    </tr>
                    {% endfor %}
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>

              <h3 style="margin-top: 28px;">Guessed instead of staying unknown ({{ wrong.abstained_to_wrong|length }})</h3>
              <p class="chart-sub">The draft said “unknown.” Checks filled in an answer that disagreed with the human label.</p>
              <div class="table-wrap">
                <table>
                  <thead>
                    <tr><th>App</th><th>Fact</th><th>Agent guess</th><th>My label</th></tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody>
                    {% for r in wrong.abstained_to_wrong %}
                    <tr>
                      <td>{{ r.app }}</td>
                      <td>{{ r.field.replace('_', ' ') }}</td>
                      <td>{{ r.after_value }}</td>
                      <td>{{ r.golden }}</td>
                    </tr>
                    {% endfor %}
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3>Apps that were hard to research</h3>
              <p class="chart-sub">Thin public docs, NDA-gated specs, or unusual shapes (CLI tools, open-source projects).</p>
              <div class="table-wrap">
                <table>
                  <thead>
                    <tr><th>App</th><th>Group</th><th class="num">Score</th><th class="num">Unknown facts</th></tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody>
                    {% for a in wrong.hard_apps %}
                    <tr>
                      <td><button type="button" class="chip" data-jump-app="{{ a.app_id }}">{{ a.app }}</button></td>
                      <td>{{ a.bucket.replace("_", " ") }}</td>
                      <td class="num">{{ a.score }}/10</td>
                      <td class="num">{{ a.eval_unknowns }}/6</td>
                    </tr>
                    {% endfor %}
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>

              <h3 style="margin-top: 28px;">Facts still marked unknown (all 100 apps)</h3>
              <div class="table-wrap">
                <table>
                  <thead><tr><th>Fact</th><th class="num">Unknown count</th></tr></thead>
                  <tbody>
                    {% for u in wrong.unknown_by_field %}
                    <tr><td>{{ u.field.replace('_', ' ') }}</td><td class="num">{{ u.unknown_count }}</td></tr>
                    {% endfor %}
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 7. How it was built -->
        <section id="architecture" class="chapter">
          <div class="chapter-head">
            <div class="chapter-num">07 / How the agent works</div>
            <h2>Research first, check second, score without guessing</h2>
            <p class="lead">
              One model researches each app and must cite a docs quote. A second, independent model helps verify those answers. Readiness scores and the four build groups are calculated in plain code — no model picks the score.
            </p>
          </div>

